.TH "SLIPWAY-SYNC" "1" "2026-09-30" "slipway 0.1.0" "Slipway Manual"
.SH NAME
slipway\-sync \- Fetch projects and fast\-forward their branches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "slipway sync"
.I "[NAME... | project/NAME...]"\&
.RI [ flags ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetch each selected project and fast\-forward its branch.
.PP
Runs in every project of the current group, in the projects named, in the ones a label selector matches, or with \-\-all\-groups in every project. Each project is fetched as slipway fetch fetches it and compared with its manifest as slipway diff compares it, and its checked\-out branch is fast\-forwarded onto its upstream when the branch tracks an upstream that still exists, is behind it without commits of its own, has no staged, unstaged or conflicted changes and no merge, rebase or other operation in progress. Untracked files do not stop it, and git refuses a fast\-forward that would overwrite one. Sync never merges, rebases, stashes, resets, switches a branch or changes a remote.
.PP
A project whose spec.syncPolicy is FetchOnly is only fetched, and one whose spec.paused is true is left alone: no git command runs in it. A project pinned by spec.revision is fast\-forwarded up to that commit instead of its upstream, only when its upstream holds the commit, never past it, and never moved back to it.
.PP
Each project prints one line, one of the results listed below, with a reason in parentheses and the details under it. The parallel setting caps how many projects fetch at once, fast\-forwards run one at a time, and the results print in the order the projects are listed.
.PP
With \-\-dry\-run nothing is fetched or written: the plan is made from the last fetch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-selector\fR \fIEXPR\fR
Selector (label query) to filter on, supports '=', '==', '!=', 'in', 'notin' (e.g. \-l key1=value1,key2=value2,key3 in (value3)). Matching objects must satisfy all of the specified label constraints.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-all\-groups\fR
If present, sync every project across all groups. The group in the current configuration is ignored even if specified with \-\-group.
.TP
\fB\-\-prune\fR
Before fetching, remove any remote\-tracking references that no longer exist on the remote.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would change and write nothing.
.SH RESULTS
When more than one project ran, a count of the results closes the run on stderr. With \-\-dry\-run every line and the count end in (dry run). Ctrl\-C stops the git processes slipway started and exits with status 130; a fast\-forward it stops ends as one stopped at the deadline.
.TP
\fBfast\-forwarded\fR
The branch moved. For a move onto the upstream, the detail names the commits it gained, as main a1b2c3d..e4f5a6b (3 commits), and the command that undoes the move; a move up to a spec.revision pin ends in (to the pinned revision).
.TP
\fBfetched\fR
The fetch of a FetchOnly project moved refs; the refs follow as in slipway fetch.
.TP
\fBunchanged\fR
The branch stayed where it was and nothing blocked it; the fetch may still have moved remote\-tracking refs.
.TP
\fBskipped (Reason)\fR
The branch stayed where it was: a blocker stopped it, under the name slipway diff gives it; git refused the fast\-forward (WouldOverwrite for untracked files in the way, WouldLoseChanges for local changes git status does not show, Busy for a lock another git process holds on the index, HEAD or the branch, NotFastForward for a branch that gained a commit since the check); or the project was skipped before its fetch, as in slipway fetch (Missing, NotARepo, Unsafe, Unknown, NoRemote, LocalUpstream).
.TP
\fBpaused\fR
spec.paused is true, so no git command ran in the project.
.TP
\fBdenied (Reason)\fR
The fetch or the fast\-forward needed a password, a passphrase or a host key (AuthRequired), as in slipway fetch.
.TP
\fBfailed (Reason)\fR
The fetch or the fast\-forward ran past networkTimeout (Timeout), used a transport protocols leaves out (ProtocolNotAllowed), or git failed for another reason (Unknown). A fast\-forward stopped at the deadline leaves the branch where it was, but the files git had already written stay in the working tree, and the detail names the command that lists them.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Every selected project was fast\-forwarded, fetched, left unchanged, skipped or paused.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Runtime error, such as a missing resource or an unreadable manifest, or a project whose fetch or fast\-forward was denied or failed.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Usage error: unknown command, unknown flag or invalid argument.
.TP
\fB130\fR
Interrupted by SIGINT.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Sync every project in the current group
slipway sync
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Sync every project in every group
slipway sync \-A
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Sync two projects of the work group
slipway sync api web \-n work
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Show what sync would do from the last fetch, without contacting any remote
slipway sync \-A \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
